// Title: COM Hijack via Sdclt
// Sigma ID: 07743f65-7ec9-404a-a519-913db7118a8d
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Omkar Gudhate
// Date: 2020-09-27 | Modified: 2023-09-28
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, T1546, T1548
// Description: Detects changes to 'HKCU\Software\Classes\Folder\shell\open\command\DelegateExecute'
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - http://blog.sevagas.com/?Yet-another-sdclt-UAC-bypass
//   - https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/47696
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_comhijack_sdclt.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\Software\\Classes\\Folder\\shell\\open\\command\\DelegateExecute"
